2:T71e,{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"How much does a kitchen fitter cost per day in the UK?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"As a rough guide, a kitchen fitter may charge around £200 to £350 per day. Rates vary according to location, experience, project complexity and which additional trades are included. Every project differs, so get a free, no-obligation quote for accurate pricing."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How much does it cost to fit a kitchen excluding the units?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"As a rough guide, labour-only fitting may cost roughly £1,500 to £3,000 for a small straightforward kitchen, rising to £6,000 or more for a larger or more complex renovation. Every project differs, so get a free, no-obligation quote for accurate pricing."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Does a kitchen fitter connect appliances?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Some fitters include appliance installation or connections, while others charge separately or require specialist trades. Ask for each appliance and connection to be listed in the quotation."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Is it cheaper to keep the same kitchen layout?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Often, yes. Keeping sinks, appliances and services in their existing positions can reduce plumbing, electrical and preparation work, although the condition of the room still affects the final cost."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How long does it take to fit a kitchen?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"A straightforward installation may take several days, while a full renovation involving plumbing, electrics, tiling, flooring and decorating can take considerably longer. Your fitter should provide a project-specific estimate."}}]}7:["slug","how-much-does-a-kitchen-fitter-cost-uk","d"]
